                    <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse1">
                        What should I include on a landscaping invoice?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        A landscaping invoice should include your business name, license/insurance number (if applicable), client details, service date and address, description of work (e.g., "lawn mowing – 0.5 acre", "spring clean-up – leaf removal, pruning", "patio installation – 200 sq ft"), itemized labor (hours × rate), materials (plants, mulch, stone), equipment rental, any travel fees, taxes, deposit paid, balance due, and payment terms.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq2">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse2">
                        Is this landscaping invoice generator really free?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        Yes! RatPDF's invoice generator is completely free for landscapers. No hidden fees, subscriptions, or watermarks. Create unlimited invoices and download them as PDF files at no cost.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
